{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016nPeSP4RYDWT4i5QH2hyR8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully to determine what tasks to propose.\n\n## Project Summary\n\nThis is a Go reimplementation of GNU coreutils/moreutils, verified via differential testing. The pipeline is: extract specs from C source → specify (SRD) → synthesize (AI code gen) → verify (differential testing).\n\n## Current State\n\nLooking at the `requirement_states` field, I need to find which SRDs have requirements with status \"ready\" — these are the ones that need tasks proposed.\n\nLet me list all SRDs with ready requirements:\n\n1. **srd004-ts** — All requirements ready (R1.1-R10.3) — release 15.0\n\n\n2. **srd071-numfmt** — R3.1-R4.4 ready — release 08.1\n3. **srd072-od** — R1.1-R4.4 ready — release 08.1\n4. **srd073-printf** — R1.1-R4.4 ready — release 08.1\n5. **srd074-sha224sum** — R1.1-R4.3 ready — release 09.0\n6. **srd075-sha384sum** — R1.1-R4.3 ready — release 09.0\n7. **srd076-b2sum** — R1.1-R4.3 ready — release 09.0\n8. **srd077-cksum** — R1.1-R3.3 ready — release 09.0\n9. **srd078-sum** — R1.1-R3.3 ready — release 09.0\n10. **srd079-base32** — R1.1-R3.3 ready — release 09.1\n11. **srd080-base64** — R1.1-R3.3 ready — release 09.1\n12. **srd081-basenc** — R1.1-R3.4 ready — release 09.1\n13. **srd082-stat** — multiple ready — release 10.0\n14. **srd083-truncate** — R1.1-R3.3 ready — release 10.0\n15. **srd084-link** — R1.1-R2.3 ready — release 10.0\n16. **srd085-sync** — continuing the list... Continuing through the remaining utilities in the sequence, covering who, pinky, shred, chroot, install, tsort, pathchk, and test across releases 11.1 through 12.1. Looking at the release status for these additional tools, I'm seeing a pattern where most are ready across multiple requirement levels with releases ranging from 13.0 to 15.0. Now I need to identify which releases have incomplete code by checking the code_status section, particularly focusing on the earliest one that still needs work. Continuing through the rest of the SRDs with pending requirements, I see they span from rel09.1 through rel12.1, covering utilities like basenc, stat, truncate, file permission commands, user management tools, and various other utilities across the remaining releases.\n\nLooking at the next batch, I notice srd104 through srd114 map to later releases, with some jumping ahead to rel15.0 for stty and ptx. The earliest release that's actually ready to move forward is 08.1, which needs numfmt, od, and printf — though numfmt already has requirements R1.1 through R2.4 completed. I see that srd072-od and srd073-printf both have all requirements ready across R1.1-R4.4. Since I'm limited to 4 tasks and need to focus on the earliest incomplete release, I need to figure out the weight constraints—but I don't have the actual weights from requirements.yaml, so I'll assume the default weight of 1 per requirement, which means I can fit up to 4 requirements per task.\n\nFor srd071-numfmt with 8 ready requirements, I'd split them into two tasks of 4 each. But srd072-od and srd073-printf each have 16 ready requirements, which would require multiple tasks each—and I'm quickly hitting my 4-task limit just trying to cover the incomplete requirements in 08.1.\n\nLet me focus on what makes sense: continue numfmt with the next 8 requirements, then start od with its first 8. That gives me 4 tasks total, which fits the batch constraint. I need to check whether there are any contract requirements I should verify before proposing these. I'm realizing that cmd/ packages are executables rather than libraries, so they don't follow the same contract pattern as pkg/ packages—the SRD itself serves as the contract. Since package_contracts only lists pkg/ packages, I don't think cmd/ packages need separate contract tasks before implementation.\n\nSo I'm settling on four tasks: two for cmd/numfmt covering requirements R3.1-R3.4 and R4.1-R4.4, and two for cmd/od covering R1.1-R1.4 and R2.1-R2.4. Each task has a weight of 4, which checks out against the requirement weights.\n\nNow I need to write the actual task descriptions. The constraint is that I can't use tools, so I'll need to reference the SRDs in the required_reading section and let the stitch agent pull the details from there. The project context only gives me requirement states, not the full SRD content, so I'll work with what I know about numfmt and od from the roadmap descriptions and write task descriptions that point the agent to the right SRD sections.\n\nLooking at the existing commit pattern for numfmt, the titles follow the format \"[stitch] cmd/numfmt: srd071 R2.1-R2.4\", so I should maintain that structure for the new tasks covering R3.1-R4.4.\n\nFor numfmt, I'm planning two continuation tasks that modify the existing main and test files. Then for od, I'm creating a new utility starting with R1.1-R1.4, followed by R2.1-R2.4 that builds on the initial implementation.\n\nThe dependency structure is straightforward: numfmt tasks chain together, od tasks chain together, but the two utilities are independent of each other. I'm thinking through what R3 and R4 likely cover for numfmt since R1 and R2 are already complete—probably more advanced formatting features.\n\nFor the YAML structure, I need to distinguish between modifying existing numfmt files versus creating new od files from scratch. The stitch agent will need clear guidance on which files to work with and what action to take on each one.\n\nWriting task descriptions now... I need to add the fourth requirement to complete the set, then lay out the design decisions for how I'll extend the existing implementation while maintaining compatibility. I'm planning to use differential testing against the reference binary and install the SIGPIPE handler at startup. The acceptance criteria cover compilation, test passage, full requirement implementation, and test coverage for all four new features. I'm looking at the design decisions and acceptance criteria for the numfmt implementation—I need to extend the existing code rather than rewrite it, use differential testing against gnumfmt as the reference, and install the SIGPIPE handler at startup. The tests need to pass compilation and the full test suite, with all R4.1-R4.4 requirements covered by differential tests.\n\nNow I'm reviewing the od utility task, which requires creating the main implementation and differential tests for R1.1-R1.4 requirements from the SRD specification, following the same patterns established for numfmt. Now I'm moving on to implement the R2.1-R2.4 requirements from the same specification, which means modifying the existing od implementation and adding corresponding differential tests to cover the new functionality.\n\nWait, I need to verify what the actual reference binary is for od — GNU coreutils provides it, but I should confirm the exact name to use for the differential testing.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":48608,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":48608},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8130d263-a470-4631-8950-3a349dfaa69b","uuid":"c70299c1-a893-402e-96e1-60913f9ed0f4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_016nPeSP4RYDWT4i5QH2hyR8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: GNU coreutils have no formal specs for implementers. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity via differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `docs/specs/` (SRDs, use cases), `cmd/` (one Go binary per utility), `pkg/` (shared libs: testutils, sys, format, hashutil, sizeparse, encutil), `magefiles/` (build automation).\n\n**Current state**: 114 SRDs specified across 33 releases. Many utilities implemented in this generation run. Recent commits completed numfmt R1.1-R2.4 (tasks 5470-5471).\n\n**Current release focus**: Release 08.1 is the earliest incomplete release with ready requirements. Three utilities remain: numfmt (R3.1-R4.4 ready), od (R1.1-R4.4 ready), printf (R1.1-R4.4 ready).\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 08.1 has three not-started/partially-started utilities. numfmt is partially done (R1.1-R2.4 complete), so I continue with R3.1-R4.4. Then start od (R1.1-R2.4). printf will follow in a future batch. numfmt and od have no cross-dependency.\n\n## Weight Budget Checks\n\n- Task 0: srd071 R3.1(1) + R3.2(1) + R3.3(1) + R3.4(1) = 4 -- at limit\n- Task 1: srd071 R4.1(1) + R4.2(1) + R4.3(1) + R4.4(1) = 4 -- at limit\n- Task 2: srd072 R1.1(1) + R1.2(1) + R1.3(1) + R1.4(1) = 4 -- at limit\n- Task 3: srd072 R2.1(1) + R2.2(1) + R2.3(1) + R2.4(1) = 4 -- at limit\n\nAll within budget (assuming default weight 1).\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/numfmt: srd071 R3.1-R3.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd071-numfmt.yaml (R3.1-R3.4 requirements)\n      - cmd/numfmt/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1-R2.4)\n      - cmd/numfmt/numfmt_test.go (existing differential tests)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (SIGPIPE handler usage)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/numfmt/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R3.1-R3.4 functionality to existing numfmt implementation\n      - path: cmd/numfmt/numfmt_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for R3.1-R3.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd071 R3.1 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd071 R3.2 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd071 R3.3 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd071 R3.4 per the SRD specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Extend the existing numfmt implementation -- do not rewrite existing R1.1-R2.4 code\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use the differential testing pattern with gnumfmt as the reference binary\n      - id: D3\n        text: Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main if not already present\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./cmd/numfmt/ compiles without errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go test ./cmd/numfmt/... -count=1 passes\n      - id: AC3\n        text: All R3.1-R3.4 requirements from srd071-numfmt are implemented\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Differential tests cover R3.1-R3.4 behavior against gnumfmt\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/numfmt: srd071 R4.1-R4.4\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd071-numfmt.yaml (R4.1-R4.4 requirements)\n      - cmd/numfmt/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1-R3.4)\n      - cmd/numfmt/numfmt_test.go (existing differential tests)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/numfmt/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R4.1-R4.4 functionality to existing numfmt implementation\n      - path: cmd/numfmt/numfmt_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for R4.1-R4.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd071 R4.1 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd071 R4.2 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd071 R4.3 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd071 R4.4 per the SRD specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Extend the existing numfmt implementation -- do not rewrite existing R1.1-R3.4 code\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use the differential testing pattern with gnumfmt as the reference binary\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./cmd/numfmt/ compiles without errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go test ./cmd/numfmt/... -count=1 passes\n      - id: AC3\n        text: All R4.1-R4.4 requirements from srd071-numfmt are implemented\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Differential tests cover R4.1-R4.4 behavior against gnumfmt\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/od: srd072 R1.1-R1.4\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd072-od.yaml (R1.1-R1.4 requirements)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (SIGPIPE handler)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (differential testing framework)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/od/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: od utility -- dump files in octal and other formats\n      - path: cmd/od/od_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for R1.1-R1.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd072 R1.1 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd072 R1.2 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd072 R1.3 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd072 R1.4 per the SRD specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Use the differential testing pattern with god as the reference binary via exec.LookPath\n      - id: D2\n        text: Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main\n      - id: D3\n        text: Skip tests with t.Skip if the reference binary god is not found in PATH\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./cmd/od/ compiles without errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go test ./cmd/od/... -count=1 passes\n      - id: AC3\n        text: All R1.1-R1.4 requirements from srd072-od are implemented\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Differential tests cover R1.1-R1.4 behavior against god\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/od: srd072 R2.1-R2.4\"\n  dependency: 2\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd072-od.yaml (R2.1-R2.4 requirements)\n      - cmd/od/main.go (existing implementation covering R1.1-R1.4)\n      - cmd/od/od_test.go (existing differential tests)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/od/main.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add R2.1-R2.4 functionality to existing od implementation\n      - path: cmd/od/od_test.go\n        action: modify\n        note: Add differential tests for R2.1-R2.4\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: Implement srd072 R2.1 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R2\n        text: Implement srd072 R2.2 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R3\n        text: Implement srd072 R2.3 per the SRD specification\n      - id: R4\n        text: Implement srd072 R2.4 per the SRD specification\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: Extend the existing od implementation -- do not rewrite existing R1.1-R1.4 code\n      - id: D2\n        text: Use the differential testing pattern with god as the reference binary\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: go build ./cmd/od/ compiles without errors\n      - id: AC2\n        text: go test ./cmd/od/... -count=1 passes\n      - id: AC3\n        text: All R2.1-R2.4 requirements from srd072-od are implemented\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Differential tests cover R2.1-R2.4 behavior against god\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":48608,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":48608},"output_tokens":19,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8130d263-a470-4631-8950-3a349dfaa69b","uuid":"047cfab9-610e-44ac-924d-bcdaba76d555"}
